Title: Document update && init as the delivery sequence for refreshed defaults
Created: 2026-06-04
Author: MinhHaDuong

--- log ---
2026-06-04T09:01Z MinhHaDuong created

--- body ---
## Source
2026-06-04 conversation on migrate vs update, prompted by a live
incident: a new default label cannot reach existing stores via
`erg update` alone.

## Context
`erg update` replaces the binary; it never touches store files.
`erg init` unpacks the stock `.ergrc`, which MATERIALIZES the default
label vocabulary as literal lines under `[labels]`. Because
`effectiveLabelSet` (src/go/config.go) uses the binary's
`defaultLabels` only when `.ergrc` has no `[labels]` section, every
store initialized from stock has its vocabulary frozen-by-copy at init
time: a default added later to the binary is shadowed and never takes
effect, even after `erg update`.

The working delivery sequence is `erg update && erg init`: init's
dpkg-style 3-state compare recognizes an untouched stock `.ergrc`
(matches the `.erg-assets` stamp or a known shipped hash) as a clean
upgrade and overwrites it; a locally-edited vocabulary is preserved
with exit 2 -- the user opts in manually, which is correct.

Nothing needs backporting onto closed tickets: vocabulary additions
are purely additive and label validation reads the vocabulary, not
the ticket files.

## Fix
Document, not code. Make `update && init` discoverable as the
canonical "absorb refreshed defaults and assets" sequence:
- helpUpdate (src/go/update.go): after the existing migration-guidance
  paragraph, state that embedded-asset/default changes are delivered
  by a follow-up `erg init`, never by update itself.
- helpInit (src/go/init.go): name the sequence from the other end.
- src/go/assets/integration.md: one short subsection on keeping a
  store current (update -> init -> migrate, what each does and does
  not touch).
Keep the three wordings coherent; the CI self-coherence guard should
cover drift where applicable.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] helpUpdate names `erg init` as the asset/defaults delivery step
- [ ] helpInit mentions the `update && init` sequence
- [ ] integration.md documents the keep-current sequence and the
      .ergrc shadowing behaviour (defaults frozen-by-copy)
- [ ] make check passes